  "term": "ventral posterior cingulate cortex",
  "definition": "The ventral posterior cingulate cortex is a lower part of the posterior cingulate cortex, a brain region. In this source, it is identified as one of the areas whose functional connectivity with the amygdala changes immediately after acute stress.",
